    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug:** The `frai gate init --ci` command from the CLI was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`), even though the command works correctly when running `frai-gate init --ci` directly.\n\n**Root Cause:** Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag as an unknown option, but it wasn't being passed through to the action callback. The callback was only receiving the positional arguments, not the options.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to use `process.argv` directly instead of relying on the parsed `args` parameter from commander.js. This ensures all arguments and flags (including `--ci`) are correctly passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Updated the `gate` command action callback (lines 742-756) to extract all arguments after 'gate' from `process.argv` and pass them to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Verification:** Successfully tested the fix:\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
